invariant: INV-16
file: src/sha3.h
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha3-bmi
reason: sha3_on_instructions picks sha3_hw.c's x86-64 copy where the
  session's ch_cfg.cpu holds CH_CPU_BMI1 alone, so a session whose caller
  never said the CPU has BMI2 runs RORX, and dies of SIGILL on a CPU
  without it. The qemu lane's sha3-bmi part counts the SHA-3 calls under
  each value, and runs ML-DSA-87's vectors under CH_CPU_BMI1 alone on a
  model without BMI2, where they must pass. x86-64 alone compiles this arm
  of sha3.h.

--- old
    uint32_t both = CH_CPU_BMI1 | CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX;
--- new
    uint32_t both = CH_CPU_BMI1;
